# Code owners for the HFIG Data Vault Accelerator.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS: branch protection on `main` sets
# require_code_owner_reviews, which means an approval only counts if it comes
# from an owner named here. Without this file that setting has nothing to
# match, and any collaborator's approval would satisfy the gate.
#
# The rule is deliberately the whole repository. This accelerator's correctness
# lives in places a path-scoped rule would miss: a hashing constant, a gate's
# allowlist, an entity YAML and a bundle variable can each change behaviour in
# the lake, and several defects found here came from exactly the files nobody
# would think to scope a review to.
#
# NOTE ON SELF-APPROVAL: GitHub does not allow approving your own pull request.
# Admins are exempt from protection (enforce_admins=false) so the owner can
# still merge their own work; everyone else needs the owner's review. If a
# second owner is ever added, tighten enforce_admins and remove that exemption.

* @Adrian-Turcu
